  "title": "A 125B AI model is running on gaming PCs",
  "narration": "Someone just got a 125-billion-parameter AI model running on a normal gaming PC. Strata runs Qwen3.8-Flash-Next using your GPU, system RAM, and even SSD together. The trick is mixture-of-experts: Qwen has 125 billion parameters, but only about 6 billion activate per token. Strata keeps hot experts on the GPU and spills the rest into RAM. On an RTX 5070, the project reports up to 94 tokens per second. The catch? You still want at least 12GB of VRAM, 32GB RAM, and roughly 80GB free storage. So yes, local giant models are getting weirdly practical.",
